+## Prepare workload templates before provisioning hosts
+
+[D · g5.scope.deployment.workload_templates]
+
+The worker-image build may precompute disposable workload templates from pinned OCI
+environments and explicitly scoped committed repository inputs, so new hosts validate
+and reuse them before registration. Keep [shared platform packaging](#share-platform-packaging-across-customers):
+templates are optional rebuildable cache data, not customer-specific platform behavior.
+Distribute repository-bearing artifacts only to infrastructure authorized for those
+sources; [repository seed eligibility](../software_architecture/worker_host.g5.md#seed-only-authorized-repository-members)
+separately governs guest exposure. Build-time caches contain no credentials or working
+state. Hosts retain runtime identity, capacity, isolation and readiness checks when
+using prebuilt data; missing or incompatible templates do not bypass those checks.
+
