+### Keep accelerated workload storage guest-private and disposable
+
+[D · g5.architecture.build_scratch]
+
+For new opt-in Linux microVM boots, place the complete workload on one private,
+ephemeral block filesystem within the published scratch capacity. Preserve guest
+paths, creation permissions, isolation and the independent read-only [runtime bundle](runtime.g5.md#the-platform-supplies-its-complete-runtime).
+Prepare a pristine image before guest ownership; finish fresh workspace import and
+per-VM configuration during bootstrap before hooks, workload execution or readiness.
+Only pristine image templates and access-scoped committed repository seeds may be shared;
+each guest writes a private clone. Repository seeds follow the [seed contract](#seed-only-authorized-repository-members). The
+host template owner bounds cached variants and accounts for full-slot capacity plus
+template preparation before activation. The host never mounts a guest-written filesystem.
+Existing [fresh materialization](runtime.g5.md#every-start-builds-a-fresh-workspace-root),
+[complete Git receipts](durability.g5.md#only-verified-complete-capture-advances-recovery)
+and [exit-proven disposal](runtime.g5.md#delete-a-workspace-root-when-its-vm-is-released)
+remain authoritative; no guest image is retained for reuse or recovery. Reject
+unsupported boot modes or preparation failures rather than silently falling back.
+Qualify startup, workflow/recovery, full-slot capacity and block flush behavior
+before widening rollout; disk sizing and custody retain their existing owners.
+
+### Seed only authorized repository members
+
+[D · g5.architecture.workload_repo_seed]
+
+A deployment-built repository seed is a rebuildable accelerator, never a saved workspace.
+Bind it to the resolved environment/capacity/layout and exact authorized organization,
+cache generation, with every seeded member exactly matching an authorized repository
+ID, root and Git endpoint; additional workspace members are freshly imported. Never
+attach its disk to a nonmatching workspace: deleting files does not erase raw blocks.
+Build only from pinned committed sources, without credentials or guest-written state.
+Before attachment, require each baseline commit in the independently restored authorized
+repository object store; an absent baseline is a generic miss.
+Keep [fresh materialization](runtime.g5.md#every-start-builds-a-fresh-workspace-root) and
+complete receipt restoration on the host; bootstrap must transform the private seed
+clone into that exact restored tree before hooks or readiness, including deletions and
+Git metadata. Publish the immutable disk and its comparison baseline together. Bound
+the owner to one generic and one repository variant, with staging and full-slot capacity
+accounted for; mismatches retain the generic path and failed import cannot become Ready.
+Enable repository seeds for rollout only after demonstrating a startup benefit and
+qualifying the affected workspace flows on the target workload.
+
